1	/**
2	 * /api/agents — live agent activity feed for the desktop Live panel.
3	 *
4	 * Konrad wanted the Claude Code CLI's transparency: for every agent that is
5	 * actively burning tokens right now, show ELAPSED runtime, tokens in/out
6	 * (including cache hits — that's where the real cost signal lives), the
7	 * running USD spend, the model powering it, and what tool it's touching
8	 * this second. The old Live panel showed none of that.
9	 *
10	 * Two concurrency systems, one endpoint. Distinguished by `kind`:
11	 *
12	 *   • System B — durable forge-control tasks. Each is a separate `claude`
13	 *     CLI process (its own row in `runs`), survives session cycles, has a
14	 *     UUID, spend, heartbeat. These are the "workers". `kind: "run"`.
15	 *
16	 *   • System A — Claude Code sub-agents (Task tool). They live INSIDE one
17	 *     System B run's CLI process, share its session, and vanish when the
18	 *     parent exits. Detected on the wire via `parent_tool_use_id` — the
19	 *     executor's onEvent stamps every streamed event with it and registers
20	 *     Task-tool spawns in `runs.thread[].meta.spawns_subagent_role`.
21	 *     `kind: "subagent"`, nested under `run.subagents`.
22	 *
23	 * The UI renders System B as top-level rows and System A as indented
24	 * children — mirroring the actual "workers vs. threads inside a worker"
25	 * split so the concurrency model is legible at a glance.
26	 */
