## 4. Where task notifications live (answer: nowhere)

### Persistence path

Threads are **NOT** JSON files. They are a `jsonb` column: **PostgreSQL `content_forge` DB, table `public.runs`, column `thread jsonb`** — array of `{role, content, ts, kind?, meta?}`. Schema comment at `forge-control/src/db/runs.ts:1-11`; DDL at `db/migrations/0021_ai_os_tables.sql` (~line 85) + `db/migrations/0031_runs_archived.sql`.

Writers:
- `forge-control/src/executor.ts:393` `appendThreadEntry(id, entry)` — the streaming path; called at lines 588, 813, 816, 819, 867, 918.
- `forge-control/src/db/runs.ts` `appendMessage(...)` — user turns, canvas deltas, continue markers. Called from `routes/chat.ts:202, 215, 245` and `lib/telegram-bridge.ts:240`.

Readers: `getRun` → `routes/chat.ts:140` (`GET /api/chat/:id`) and `:79` (`GET /api/chat/:id/events`).

### The gap

Async agent completion notifications from the Claude Code CLI **are silently dropped by the stream parser**. `/opt/ai-os/workspace/projects/8ea0cc08-28d9-4301-9f28-c98e1c5d6838/forge-control/src/lib/cc-runner.ts:417-429`:

```ts
      } else if (evt.type === "user") {
        const msg = evt.message as { content?: StreamBlock[] } | undefined;
        for (const block of msg?.content ?? []) {
          if (block.type === "tool_result") {
            opts.onEvent({
              type: "tool_result",
              toolUseId: block.tool_use_id,
              text: blockContentToText(block.content),
              isError: block.is_error === true,
              parentToolUseId,
            });
          }
        }
      }
```

Only `tool_result` blocks inside a `user` event are forwarded. Task-completion notifications (which arrive as `text` blocks on synthetic `user` events) hit no branch → no `CcEvent` → no `appendThreadEntry` → nothing in `runs.thread`. `CcEvent.type` is a closed union of exactly four values (cc-runner.ts:170-188): `"init" | "assistant_text" | "tool_call" | "tool_result"`. There is no notification event type.

DB verification: tracing agentIds `aa4d88309ba41e8a0` and `a28e674987f417daf` (both spawned in the live operator run `3853c154-e07b-4378-9313-2b34f4a33342`) through the whole thread returns **only** the launch `tool_result` entries — no completion entry ever appears. `SELECT DISTINCT role, kind` over every thread in the DB returns exactly 7 combinations, none of them notification-shaped:

```
system|text | user|text | system|error | system|stuck_notice | tool|tool_call | tool|tool_result | assistant|text
```

Separately, `queueNotification()` (`forge-control/src/db/notifications.ts:39`, drained by `lib/telegram-bridge.ts:307-318`) is a **Telegram-only** outbound queue for run-level outcomes — it writes to the `notifications` table, never to `runs.thread`, and never reaches the web UI.

