## Summary of the seams for a Bash/Agent-aware renderer

| Concern | Location |
|---|---|
| Add per-tool renderers | `AssistantThread.tsx:127` → `tools: { by_name: { Bash: …, Agent: … }, Fallback: ToolCallRow }` |
| Access to raw `meta` in the renderer | Not available today — `thread-mapping.ts:88-97` drops everything except `tool_use_id`, `tool`, `input`. `parent_tool_use_id`, `is_error` on the call, `model`, `usage` are all discarded. |
| Distinguish subagent vs. operator work in the transcript | Requires threading `meta.parent_tool_use_id` through `ToolCallPart` in `thread-mapping.ts:15-22` |
| Task-notification entries | Do not exist. Would need a new `CcEvent` type in `cc-runner.ts:170` + a branch in the `evt.type === "user"` loop at `cc-runner.ts:417-429` + a new `kind` in both `ThreadEntry` definitions (`forge-control/src/db/runs.ts:43`, `forge-control-web/app/api.ts:586`) + a `role`/`kind` branch in `thread-mapping.ts`. |

